    <h2>Initiative 1: Modernizing a Print-First Brand for Digital Screens</h2>

    <h3>The Problem</h3>
    <p>The original ExtraCare brand identity was designed years ago for print circulars and static store banners. When digital usage accelerated, product teams across the company struggled to adapt those rigid guidelines to modern software. Squads began designing their own ad-hoc web banners, app headers, and icons. The result was a disjointed experience that diluted brand equity and confused customers moving between their phones and our store aisles.</p>

    <h3>The Strategic Shift</h3>
    <p>I took the initiative to modernize our print brand standards into a digital-first design language. Rather than simply porting over static images, I overhauled typography hierarchies, color contrast scales, and spatial systems to ensure accessibility and responsive flexibility across desktop, tablet, and mobile breakpoints—all while preserving the core brand recognition customers trusted.</p>

    <h2>Initiative 2: Creative Direction for the Nationwide Gamification Launch</h2>

    <h3>The Challenge</h3>
    <p>When the loyalty organization decided to test gamification to build daily customer routines, we faced a major organizational risk: marketing planned an aggressive in-store and email campaign, while digital product squads were developing the in-app interactive features. Without a unifying creative lead, the customer would encounter one visual style in the store aisle and a completely different visual language inside the app.</p>

    <h3>The Unifying Strategy</h3>
    <p>I served as the central creative strategist connecting these disparate squads. I established an overarching visual and conceptual framework that spanned three core touchpoints:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Physical In-Store Assets:</strong> Partnered directly with the Store Experience team to direct overhead banners, aisle blades, stanchions, and floor decals as awareness entry points.</li>
      <li><strong>Lifecycle Marketing &amp; CRM:</strong> Collaborated with marketing operations to ensure consistent tone, typography, and visual assets across high-volume email and push notification campaigns.</li>
      <li><strong>Digital Product UI:</strong> Led the design of every interactive asset inside the mobile app, which established the visual benchmark for the other teams to follow.</li>
    </ul>

