    <h2>Leadership Retrospective</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Brand Consistency Builds Customer Trust:</strong> When a shopper sees the same visual cue on an in-store shelf blade, in a morning push notification, and inside the mobile checkout cart, cognitive load drops and confidence rises.</li>
      <li><strong>Creative Direction Requires Operational Empathy:</strong> Directing brand strategy across physical stores and digital apps means respecting each medium’s unique constraints—whether it’s print ink budgets and store fixture durability or mobile render speeds and accessibility contrast ratios.</li>
      <li><strong>The Creative Lead as the Organizational Glue:</strong> Large organizations naturally drift into departmental silos. A design leader must proactively step into the center, align competing roadmaps, and ensure that the final customer journey feels intentional and unified.</li>
    </ol>
